    "formula": "A(x)=x^2, quad A'(x)=2x",
    "text": "The thin-strip reasoning connects accumulation with differentiation. Here the area function is x squared, and its derivative returns two x. At input two, the accumulated amount changes at rate four, matching the original rate at that endpoint.",
